/*
SHORT FILM TEMPLATE — Fountain format.
Target: 1-20 pages (1 page ~= 1 minute). Shorts rarely support a full 15-beat Save the
Cat sheet — think of it as a single Sequence (see ../../02-story-structure/sequence-method.md)
or a single Story Circle rotation (../../02-story-structure/story-circle.md): ONE clean
turn, not a whole saga. Kishotenketsu (../../02-story-structure/kishotenketsu.md) is also
a strong fit for shorts that want a twist without a villain.
*/

# SHORT FILM — SINGLE TURN STRUCTURE

## Status quo
= Establish the character and their want in as few images as possible. No wasted setup.

INT./EXT. << LOCATION >> - << DAY/NIGHT >>

<< Open as close to the turn as you can. A short doesn't have pages to spare. >>

## The turn
= One clear disruption. Everything after this is consequence.

<< Scene. >>

## The consequence / climax
= The character acts (or fails to act). The turn is paid off.

<< Scene. >>

## Final image
= Leave on an image, not an explanation. Trust the cut.

<< Scene. >>

FADE OUT.

> THE END <
